\paragraph{A rank-based extension.}
With the same nesting/fixed-score conditions and one-based primary rank,
\begin{equation}
 D_S(\alpha)=\sum_{q\in\mathcal Q_S}\sum_{x\in\mathcal R_{\rm ref}(q)}
 \mathbf1\{\operatorname{rank}_{\rm P}(x)>c(\alpha)\}.
 \label{eq:6-rank-curve}
\end{equation}
Exported reference ranks could recover the whole curve from one search. The current harness instead reruns every budget; rank extraction remains future work.

